The plate is a white, angular dish, probably a side plate of about 22–25 cm along its long axis. The rice covers a patch of roughly 9 × 4 cm and is about 1.5 cm high. That is a volume of about 40–50 ml, and cooked rice at about 0.75 g/ml gives roughly 40 g. Allowing for some looser grains, I estimate 45 g.

There is also a small orange speck, probably a bit of carrot or pepper, at about 1 g. A faint yellowish residue, possibly oil or butter, is too small to count as more than about 1 g.

